{
  "_id": "phbbrdBeguilingM",
  "name": "Beguiling Magic",
  "type": "feat",
  "folder": "nRLsU9drIaxSPf82",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-eye.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You always have the @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.spells.Item.phbsplCharmPerso]{Charm Person} and @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.spells.Item.phbsplMirrorImag]{Mirror Image} spells prepared.</p><p>In addition, immediately after you cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell using a spell slot, you can cause a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself to make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the target has the &amp;Reference[Charmed] or &amp;Reference[Frightened] condition (your choice) for 1 minute. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p>Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending one use of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required).</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-yJ0pYJyjePrUp7wQ\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The <strong>Save</strong> activity includes an Active Effect for both the Charmed and Frightened status.</p><p>The <strong>Recharge with Inspiration</strong> activity restores a use of this feature.</p><p>The spells are automatically added to your sheet as Always Prepared.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
